# nr-office-quality-pipeline: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml
[workspace] members: add, right after `"crates/mixdog-office-base",`:

    "crates/mixdog-office-quality",

[workspace.dependencies]: add, right after the `mixdog-office-base = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-base" }` line:

    mixdog-office-quality = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-quality" }

## 2. native/core/Cargo.lock
Lead regenerates it offline (the build is --locked after that). The new package `mixdog-office-quality` has the
dependencies `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-office-base`, `mixdog-workspace-hack` and `serde_json` (all already in the lock; no
new crate enters it). Its dev-dependency is `mixdog-office-base` with the feature `test-support`, which the base crate
already declares.

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing: the new crate's Cargo.toml carries the `mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }`
dependency as every office crate does. If the hakari rule of the workspace wants more features unified, regenerate.

## 4. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` once the wave is merged: it adds the row
of the new set `office-pipeline` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pipeline.mjs, 1 file,
golden.json). The set's own MANIFEST.json is already written (native/core/fixtures/office-pipeline/MANIFEST.json).

## 5. Consumers (later tasks of the track, not this one)
The office tools that review and finalize a document add `mixdog-office-quality = { workspace = true }` to their own
crate and call: `pipeline::{normalize_office_review_issues, build_office_polish_plan,
evaluate_office_submission_gate, resolve_office_render_output, is_advisory_office_issue}`,
`score::score_office_release_quality`, `document_acceptance::{review_document_pages, assess_document_acceptance,
is_automated_ready, review_status, document_visual_checks}`,
`presentation_acceptance::assess_presentation_acceptance`, `checklist::evaluate_office_checklist` and
`issue::{issue, issue_with}`. All of them take and answer `serde_json::Value`s with the key order Node writes.

## 6. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no desktop fragment, no environment variable.
